      "moduleId": "02-IAM",
      "questionNumber": 3,
      "scenario": "A solutions architect is writing an IAM policy to deny access to all S3 buckets except one specific bucket named \"production-data\". Which policy element should be used?\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": \"s3:*\",\n      \"Resource\": [\n        \"arn:aws:s3:::production-data\",\n        \"arn:aws:s3:::production-data/*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Deny\",\n      \"Action\": \"s3:*\",\n      \"Resource\": \"*\",\n      \"Condition\": {\n        \"StringNotEquals\": {\n          \"s3:ResourceAccount\": \"${aws:PrincipalAccount}\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWhat is the correct approach?",
